{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/636546-2ed-blood-bonds-totally-overpowered","id":636546,"title":"[2ED] Blood Bonds - Totally Overpowered","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-22T19:43:19-07:00","id":636546,"title":"[2ED] Blood Bonds - Totally Overpowered","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/636315-beast-vampire-sas-%E2%80%98morning-after%E2%80%99-%E2%80%93-actual-play\">Run today a crossover game of <b>Beast</b> &amp; <b>Vampire</b> 2ED</a> - and I found out that <i>Vinculum</i>, Blood Bonds mechanics are totally overpowered and illogically imbalanced. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>Basically, they are &quot;instant Win Button&quot; solution for any Kindred and there no restrictions on just freshly Embraced character to make total slave from younger Prince, mages Hierarch or any non-demigod status supernatural.</b> JUST. FROM. EMBRACE.<br /> <br /> I will go here on use corebook quote to ease discussion and show mine point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Requiem 2ED</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any time a character imbibes a point or more of Vitae, it creates or reinforces a blood bond. The bond comes in three stages, usually at the first, second, and third drinks. <br /> <br /> Kindred characters can attempt to resist the bond by spending Willpower. Make a Blood Potency roll, minus the number of Vitae ingested. The Willpower point does not add to this roll. If successful, that drink does not add to the bond. However, the character suffers Vitae addiction normally. Any further attempts to resist the bond from the same vampire suffer a cumulative \u20131 die penalty; even ancient Kindred cannot resist the bond forever. Mortals have no such defense.</div> </div> </div> </div>So on crossover play I assumed that Blood Potency can be exchanged on to it's Supernatural Advantage equivalents - Primal Urge, Gnosis, Lair, etc. But it's not important here.<br /> <br /> Thing is: <b>Any non-super powerful monster character can almost surely lose the test, even after drink a tea/coffee/whatever with small dosage of freshly Embraced vampire.</b> To imbibes a point of Vitea coffee or tea is enough ( Vitea is about distilled life force, not the whole liters of blood ) and this one &quot;dosage&quot; means -1 penalty. On victim with Blood Potency 1 it means Chance Roll even if she resists by the Willpower point. On Blood Potency 4 ( level of young Prince, or mages Ruling Council and many Masters ) you <i>should</i> be able to resist with Dice Pool 3, but you still are not <b>sure</b> of it. Maybe at Blood Potency 6 you are rather safe, with Dice Pool 5 to get success to resist. <i>Maybe</i>. And each other attempt after first success is much easier, as victim is more and more willing to do the same, from Vitea Addiction and artificial fond fillings to the character. And this mechanics works from yesterday Embraced vampires giving you blood! <br /> <br /> What I mean &quot;non-super powerful monster characters&quot; are beings with Supernatural Advantage on levels 1-5 ( no superhuman stats ) - so, like 90-95% of local supernatural society. Very large majority of vampires, mages, werewolves, or any other monsters just going to lose on first roll and become living puppets of vampires.<br /> <br /> There is no reason as to why starting neonates had no Blood Bonds on Protectorate Alpha werewolves or mages Ruling Councils. When vampires maybe open about their secret to not drink one another, other monsters does not have this instant knowledge, and can fall through by this. Or does suddenly or supernatural knows all weaknesses of their splats? Even then, beings like Prometheans or Beasts, with no real society, would not know, most of the time, to not drink vampires bloods. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Basically, <b>any kind of play between vampires and non-vampires makes the non-vampires PCs slaves to Kindred. Or that dedicated Kindred players can have his freshly Embraced PC rule the mages, werewolves or any other supernatural society from shadows, having slave Hierarch or Alpha Wolf.</b> It's clearly overpowered... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <i><b>Possible solution:</b></i> <b>Resistance to Blood Bond should work as any other Mind Control resistant rolls and use Resolve + Blood Potency ( or equivalents ) as Dice Pool.</b> Using second Trait in resistant makes that vampire character just cannot take ones free will on first drink ( even starting characters will have like 3-4 in resist Dice Pool, so the should pass ) and superhuman monsters elders would be mostly unaffected. Also, high Resolve characters would be rather safe to <i>multiple</i> Blood interactions from the same Kindred, and this mean that our political driven monster characters will much more willing to interact with vampires, falsely confident they can resist call of Blood much easier. What a beautiful self-deception. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Win-Win scenario, I think.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T19:47:28-07:00","id":636569,"title":"","content":"Vinculum is a dangerous, twisted thing for a reason.<br /> <br /> Making other supernaturals drink your blood in such large numbers is also not nearly as easy as you make it sound*, and it takes more than a stage 1 or even stage 2 bond to foster any kind of reliable loyalty or servitude.<br /> <br /> The overpowered utility you are attributing to it is completely illusory and unjustified.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">*And common sense is REALLY all it takes to be <i>suspicious of drinking an undead monster's blood.</i></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 08-22-2015, 10:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T19:51:52-07:00","id":636574,"title":"","content":"Nah, it's fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T20:03:42-07:00","id":636580,"title":"","content":"Yeah I think you under-estimate the difficulty of getting 3 drinks from others. Remember, you can't really store the vitae in things ahead of time (It goes inert too fast). So you basically have to be able to slight of hand it and otherwise disguise what your doing. And well, the Prince won't be drinking anything you offer, (Why the hell would they?). There is the whole distrust thing that occurs across templates also, so they would be cautious at best.<br /> <br /> In theory it sounds super powerful, but in practice it is far less. Also, it isn't dominate. They can resist, but you've got a lot of bonuses to convince them (Perfect impression (faster rolls to convince), +3 to social actions/disciplines). Basically it just amounts to being able to easily be talked into something, not total subservience. They're still not likely to go do totally radical things contrary to their own well being. That takes conditioning with proper handling of dominate or long term use of Vitae Addiction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T20:13:33-07:00","id":636585,"title":"","content":"As far as mages are concerned, this is a mental effect going against a splat where over 1/5th of its supernatural population has the ability to detect such things. So a vampire trying to blood bond any prominent member of a mage hierarchy is probably going to be found out, tracked down, and dealt with fairly swiftly. Also, the effects of the blood bond should be able to be mitigated (though the blood bond itself is unlikely to be able to be removed directly) by proper use of the Mind arcanum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T20:20:48-07:00","id":636591,"title":"","content":"I still think it would be pretty awesome to manifest vitae addiction as a goetic demon and unleash it on Elysium.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T21:13:56-07:00","id":636635,"title":"","content":"Either a)You're doing it wrong, or b) you're players are just that damn good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T22:22:01-07:00","id":636690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/636546-2ed-blood-bonds-totally-overpowered?p=636569#post636569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vinculum is a dangerous, twisted thing for a reason.<br /> <br /> Making other supernaturals drink your blood in such large numbers is also not nearly as easy as you make it sound*, and it takes more than a stage 1 or even stage 2 bond to foster any kind of reliable loyalty or servitude.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">*And common sense is REALLY all it takes to be <i>suspicious of drinking an undead monster's blood.</i></span></div> </div> </div> </div>But given tea or coffee by your host is <b>not</b> suspicious, even if he is vampire. Giving few drops of Blood to the drinks is pop culture honored tradition, and at least in mine quick reading of the rules - enough to deliver one portion of Vitea itself.<br /> <br /> By the example of V usage in <b>True Blood</b>:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wq9VFAmQYtI\" data-code=\"wq9VFAmQYtI\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/wq9VFAmQYtI/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Ingesting few drops on first night, few drops on second, and in three nights vampires made rest of their starting group ( with Supernatural Advantages 1 ) loving him slaves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/636546-2ed-blood-bonds-totally-overpowered?p=636580#post636580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah I think you under-estimate the difficulty of getting 3 drinks from others. Remember, you can't really store the vitae in things ahead of time (It goes inert too fast). So you basically have to be able to slight of hand it and otherwise disguise what your doing. And well, the Prince won't be drinking anything you offer, (Why the hell would they?). There is the whole distrust thing that occurs across templates also, so they would be cautious at best.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but once you got PC to give in to Stage 1 Blood Bond, rest is easy - just use the feelings character have to make here get more blood. And paranoia angle in vampires, mages and werewolf could work, but what about Promethans and Beasts, that do not have extensive society to give them advice &quot;do not drink from vampires&quot;?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/636546-2ed-blood-bonds-totally-overpowered?p=636580#post636580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In theory it sounds super powerful, but in practice it is far less. Also, it isn't dominate. They can resist, but you've got a lot of bonuses to convince them (Perfect impression (faster rolls to convince), +3 to social actions/disciplines). Basically it just amounts to being able to easily be talked into something, not total subservience. They're still not likely to go do totally radical things contrary to their own well being. That takes conditioning with proper handling of dominate or long term use of Vitae Addiction.</div> </div> </div> </div>They can be talked in to something - like drinking coffee or tea when proposed. It want kill them, does it? And Blood Bonded so much like their new &quot;master&quot;...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ophidimancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/636546-2ed-blood-bonds-totally-overpowered?p=636591#post636591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still think it would be pretty awesome to manifest vitae addiction as a goetic demon and unleash it on Elysium.</div> </div> </div> </div>I want to run it! Yeah, officially steal this plot line for mine next <b>Mage</b>/<b>Vampire</b> crossover! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-23-2015, 01:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T22:38:07-07:00","id":636694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/636546-2ed-blood-bonds-totally-overpowered?p=636690#post636690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But given tea or coffee by your host is <b>not</b> suspicious, even if he is vampire. Giving few drops of Blood to the drinks is pop culture honored tradition, and at least in mine quick reading of the rules - enough to deliver one portion of Vitea itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>I absolutely do not think that vitae is some kind of tasteless, odorless substance that you can trick people into drinking... more than once. An unwary guest might drink your bloody coffee, but they're likely to notice something's wrong when there's some kind of black, sickly-sweet sludge floating around in their coffee, and they suddenly have a crush on the person who gave it to them. Supernatural beings in particular are likely to know, or at least suspect, that magic mind control is a thing, and are unlikely to react with hugs and kisses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T22:51:45-07:00","id":636696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/636546-2ed-blood-bonds-totally-overpowered?p=636694#post636694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I absolutely do not think that vitae is some kind of tasteless, odorless substance that you can trick people into drinking... more than once. An unwary guest might drink your bloody coffee, but they're likely to notice something's wrong when there's some kind of black, sickly-sweet sludge floating around in their coffee, and they suddenly have a crush on the person who gave it to them. Supernatural beings in particular are likely to know, or at least suspect, that magic mind control is a thing, and are unlikely to react with hugs and kisses.</div> </div> </div> </div>But then victim already have crush on the person giving it. Adding some Persuasion check, and she will repeat it. ( Vampire get's +1 to Social Rolls and lowering Doors on the victim then. ) So victim gets once again in to drinking &quot;Bloody coffee&quot; and she is on Stage 2 Blood Bonds... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T23:23:29-07:00","id":636725,"title":"","content":"I distinctly recall reading in 1st Edition that the Vinculum does not work on other major templates, only on vampires and mortals. Is this still a thing in 2nd Edition? I must admit I haven't had the chance to read my copy of 2nd Ed fully yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T23:35:29-07:00","id":636730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zooroos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/636546-2ed-blood-bonds-totally-overpowered?p=636725#post636725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I distinctly recall reading in 1st Edition that the Vinculum does not work on other major templates, only on vampires and mortals. Is this still a thing in 2nd Edition? I must admit I haven't had the chance to read my copy of 2nd Ed fully yet.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The FAQ answers that, yes, other major supernatural templates can be blood bonded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T00:02:41-07:00","id":636770,"title":"","content":"Do note that even if you somehow get past:<br /> How incredibly quickly blood loses potency in 2e (I'd argue against dosing most foods or drinks due to the vitae not wanting to mix properly)<br /> The natural suspicion of vampires, particularly vampires (who do not eat or drink) having food and drink on hand to give to non-vampiric guests<br /> The fact that you have to do it three times in a row<br /> <br /> Then you still have problems. People under vinculum are not mind-controlled slaves. They are people who are obsessively, destructively infatuated with the vampire. Maybe the vampire can give them orders, but what's stopping someone with Vinculum from seeing that Touchstone the vampire loves so much, getting jealous, and trying to take them out of the picture so the vampire will love them more? It's a magically enforced destructive relationship. It isn't Dominate. Vampires who aren't supremely careful with both who they Bond and how they handle them once bonded should find their life getting very out-of-control very quickly, and an out-of-control vampire is a dead vampire.<br /> <br /> Vinculum seems written as a double-edged sword, and I run it as a double-edged sword.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T02:14:59-07:00","id":636820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/636546-2ed-blood-bonds-totally-overpowered?p=636696#post636696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But then victim already have crush on the person giving it. Adding some Persuasion check, and she will repeat it. ( Vampire get's +1 to Social Rolls and lowering Doors on the victim then. ) So victim gets once again in to drinking &quot;Bloody coffee&quot; and she is on Stage 2 Blood Bonds... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>A crush doesn't equal stupid. If I have a crush on someone who just tried to slip me something in my drink my feelings for them become irrelevant. At that point self preservation kicks in, and the more they tried to convince me to just go with it the harder I'd nope out of that situation. I'll just argue this from a mages perspective since I know them best, but if I were having tea with a vampire, tasted something funny in my drink, and had my peripheral mage sight go off there wouldn't be a thing that vampire could do or say short of straight up mind control to keep my at the table peacefully.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T05:16:30-07:00","id":636894,"title":"","content":"In my game, I would not accept a blood bond through a cup of tea of coffee. Let's see why:<br /> <br /> 1st, I absolutly now that vitae points and lethal points are abstract and I always thought that giving them numerical values as canon is wrong. But still, it can help us to evaluate proportions in relation to one another, while recognizing that the result should not be a strong golden rule.<br /> <br /> 2st, let's try to evaluate in real values what it means. 1 vitae = 1 lethal damage. You can kill a human by drinking him dry. An average human = 5 damage. An average human has also, from biological standarts, 5 to 6 liters of blood. We can approximately say that 1 vitae = 1 liter of blood. To avoid making this a canon, let's say it can depend from the narrative context (defined by the ST or a dialogic construction between ST and player), and that 1 vitae = +_ from 1/3 to 3 liters of blood. Generally, specially during the game, it's not useful to give real life numbers to these conceptual indicators, but let's do it here for the purpose. As a blood bond equals 1 vitae. It means that your cup of tea or coffee should contain at least, in our largest case, 1/3 liters. It means you don't have coffee in your cup, if you fill it with blood.<br /> <br /> 3st, vitae is not blood. It is a magical transformation of blood through the vampire's being. It has more potency. It has a magical taste. I would say that the blood does not liquefy easily in a liquid. One cannot dring half a cup of tea without knowing what he's drinking. The magical potency of the vitae is stronger that the blackness of your ethiopian coffee. Of course, there's the taste, the magical appealing to the taste of vitae. You feel you're drinking something very special, but you bloody know what it is : not blood, but something that you can directly categorizye to &quot;something f*kin weird that is link to human blood&quot;.<br /> <br /> These are to me 2 good reasons to make the blood bond a plot device (it is difficult to do it, it does not only require a good roll or a wise scene, it requires a whole machination if you don't physically or magically force your target). Btw, I would use the Social Maneuvering System before letting anything that has such a consequence on the game to go.<br /> <br /> With an exception of course : the blood bound the PC is making is really good for the story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":824,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/824-araknee","user":"Araknee","date":". 08-23-2015, 08:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/824-araknee","name":"Araknee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar824_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T06:10:33-07:00","id":636919,"title":"","content":"An average human has 7 vitae in them, not 5.<br /> <br /> 5 is the lowest an adult character can <i>have</i>, period.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T06:39:41-07:00","id":636931,"title":"","content":"The analysis has problems. The bound can kill, much less take any action against, the binder at any stage of the bond, so I wouldn't describe the bound as a puppet. In vampire society, creating a blood bond would not be seen as bad, but anyone else would. If you blood bind a werewolf then the rest of the pack will notice and they will ash you. The same logic applies to most of the other supernaturals. That assumes the victim doesn't notice what is going on and kill the vampire. Most supernaturals would do just that when they start to realize a vampire is manipulating them into magically loving the vampire. The great advantage of a blood bond comes from the victim not knowing they are bound to a vampire or, if a vampire, the fact that vampires look negatively at the bound rather than the binder. Supernatural victims are not likely to be ignorant of a vampire's nature for long. The knowledge of blood bonds would spread quickly among supernatural communities soon after a member falls victim to one. Beasts are especially vulnerable because they are less antagonistic towards vampires. Beasts should be easily screwed over by vampires. That is the nature of their gameline.<br /> <br /> Edit: Beasts that find out they are blood bound can kill the regnant without negative feedback. I guess that means they get an out-of-character bonus for their in-character vulnerability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1526,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","user":"Diggs","date":". 08-23-2015, 09:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T06:51:44-07:00","id":636972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/636546-2ed-blood-bonds-totally-overpowered#post636546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/636315-beast-vampire-sas-%E2%80%98morning-after%E2%80%99-%E2%80%93-actual-play\">Run today a crossover game of <b>Beast</b> &amp; <b>Vampire</b> 2ED</a> - and I found out that <i>Vinculum</i>, Blood Bonds mechanics are totally overpowered and illogically imbalanced. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div> Not really. Lots of people covered this, but...<br /> <br /> 1) Good luck getting people to drink your blood. Its not as easy as you think. Certainly, no Prince would just do it casually.<br /> 2) Its not an instant win button, you're just really good at convincing your thrall to do something through Social Maneuvering. Use the rules for alternative Conditions and options for a thrall doing something they don't want to.<br /> 3) Vitae breaks down fast, so you can't just slip it into a drink all the time if you can't get them to drink it right away. Waiting for someone to go to the bathroom won't work if they're in there for a long time; also, bleeding into a cup in public is slightly noticable and nasty enough to get attention. As well, people in modern day times are careful around drinks, too much chance of someone drugging you. And it still tastes of blood - people tend to notice that kind of thing, and they'll realize something is up.<br /> 4) Super powerful monsters will eventually become fully bonded if they keep drinking. Why are they still drinking? Elder Kindred need it to live, but why is anyone else? No alpha werewolf is going to sit down and let themselves be blood bonded casually.<br /> <br /> The Vinclulum is a powerful tool. However, the difficulties involved in getting anyone powerful hooked are manifold, and the social control aspect is avoidable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's clearly overpowered... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div> Going Loud is overpowered compared to non-demons. Creative Thaumaturgy is comparitively overpowered. When Beast came out, people complained that Skeleton Keys and Atavisms were overpowered. Death Raging werewolves healing all damage every turn is overpowered compared to everyone else.<br /> <br /> Every game has its focus/specialty. In that specialty, the supernaturals in question are generally the best. Werewolves are superior when it comes to pack teamwork, territory, shapeshifting and hunting (not combat, not just tracking, but many different kinds of hunting). It takes a very specific build in other games to simply match a base werewolf with no powers, and the most basic of gifts and abilities put them above the others, and they can easily adapt to any situation with the right information and time. Demons are, hands down, the best at espionage, hiding, and technology. Not only is hiding a huge advantage, but breaking from hiding gives them huge advantage (Demon Form, Going Loud, etc). Mages excell at information gathering and shielding/wards. The more a mage knows about a situation, a target, or a kind of magic, the more effective they are. Beasts are the best at seeking out other supernaturals to play with (crossover), being scary (Atavisms and Nightmares), and with Lairs (Safe Place taken to a huge extreme).<br /> <br /> A vampire's specialty is control. That's self control (riding the wave, addictions, danage resistance), mind control (a ton of their powers) and physical controls (vamps are awesome at grappling). Just being in control of any situation. No one can beat vampires when it comes to this. Few can match up as well. Even a Lair 10 beast with the social Atavisms and You Must Obey is simply outclassed by a starting vamp with Majesty 2 and Dominate 1 when it comes to social manipulation. The reason? Everyone else generally needs to open doors to get targets to do anything. Vampires simply bypass the need to open doors and go right to having the person do what they want.<br /> <br /> Removing a vampire's vinculum is basically just like ripping out the more powerful aspects of other games. Should mages lose their Creative Thaumaturgy, or Werewolves their ability to shift into Gauru or their pack totem? Strip Beasts of their Lair traits and defenses? No going full on demon?<br /> <br /> TL;DR - the Vinculum is powerful, but not more so than any other splat's specialties.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T07:04:12-07:00","id":636977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/636546-2ed-blood-bonds-totally-overpowered?p=636820#post636820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A crush doesn't equal stupid. If I have a crush on someone who just tried to slip me something in my drink my feelings for them become irrelevant. At that point self preservation kicks in, and the more they tried to convince me to just go with it the harder I'd nope out of that situation. I'll just argue this from a mages perspective since I know them best, but if I were having tea with a vampire, tasted something funny in my drink, and had my peripheral mage sight go off there wouldn't be a thing that vampire could do or say short of straight up mind control to keep my at the table peacefully.</div> </div> </div> </div> Note that, even if you had a full bond, you could still run away in this situation; the vinculum just gives a social bonus and Perfect Impression; the vampire would need several turns to open enough doors to &quot;convince&quot; you to stay, which is unlikely given that you're likely already heading out and not listening. The harder part is that you're now addicted and will crave another hit of blood. And addictions are nasty. <br /> <br /> The bond is insideous because you not only crave another hit of blood, but your artificial feelings for the vampire make you also want to be around them. Mages tend to have more willpower than a normal person, and a Mentor that'll help them out, so the mage will likely shake off the effects in time. But the feelings and cravings in the meantime will be terrible. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Araknee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/636546-2ed-blood-bonds-totally-overpowered?p=636894#post636894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2st, let's try to evaluate in real values what it means. 1 vitae = 1 lethal damage. You can kill a human by drinking him dry. An average human = 5 damage. An average human has also, from biological standarts, 5 to 6 liters of blood. We can approximately say that 1 vitae = 1 liter of blood. To avoid making this a canon, let's say it can depend from the narrative context (defined by the ST or a dialogic construction between ST and player), and that 1 vitae = +_ from 1/3 to 3 liters of blood. Generally, specially during the game, it's not useful to give real life numbers to these conceptual indicators, but let's do it here for the purpose. As a blood bond equals 1 vitae. It means that your cup of tea or coffee should contain at least, in our largest case, 1/3 liters. It means you don't have coffee in your cup, if you fill it with blood.</div> </div> </div> </div> Vitae doesn't work that way. First of all, the average person has 7 health levels, so that means 14 points worth of vitae in the average person; that changes all your math. Secondly, vitae is not defined by volume of blood, its defined by the mystical qualities of life energy stored in the blood. Or do you really think an elder with 100 vitae in his body suddenly has 33 liters worth of blood? The elder's body simply couldn't be large enough to hold that much blood! <br /> <br /> In theory, a single drop of blood can hold a full point of vitae. However, that single drop would quickly dissolve and go innert, so its kind of a moot point. But my point is mainly that you can't try and associate points of vitae to liters of blood. The Curse doesn't work that way. You have to go with what is thematically appropriate at the time.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T08:03:00-07:00","id":637017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/636546-2ed-blood-bonds-totally-overpowered?p=636972#post636972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Removing a vampire's vinculum is basically just like ripping out the more powerful aspects of other games. Should mages lose their Creative Thaumaturgy, or Werewolves their ability to shift into Gauru or their pack totem? Strip Beasts of their Lair traits and defenses? No going full on demon?<br /> <br /> TL;DR - the Vinculum is powerful, but not more so than any other splat's specialties.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand this - I really do. But controling other PCs as innate ability every race member - with Majesty 2 to the mix - is really too much. Mages players do not make slaves from werewolf players - at least, not as simple as making them drink a tea. In most situation, in crossover games, Blood Bonds will only escalate quickly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T08:04:46-07:00","id":637025,"title":"","content":"They're <i>really</i> not as powerful as you seem to think they are though. Not even close.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T09:53:17-07:00","id":637115,"title":"","content":"Majesty and Dominate can create slaves and blood bonds can make using those Disciplines easier, but all a blood bond does by itself is give a bonus to using skills that everyone can use as well as the same bonus when using Disciplines. A Mage should be able to use magic to do the same thing. A Mage might have more difficulty with the roll, but a much easier time setting up the roll. A Mage wouldn't need to trick anyone to cast the spell. Ask a Mage expert and I'm sure they can tell you how the spell could be created. Changing blood bonds, especially in a crossover game, would unnecessarily weaken vampires. If vampires are creating blood bonds all over the place then the characters must be really stupid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T10:36:09-07:00","id":637157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/636546-2ed-blood-bonds-totally-overpowered?p=637017#post637017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I understand this - I really do. But controling other PCs as innate ability every race member - with Majesty 2 to the mix - is really too much. Mages players do not make slaves from werewolf players - at least, not as simple as making them drink a tea. In most situation, in crossover games, Blood Bonds will only escalate quickly.</div> </div> </div> </div> Except it <u><b><i>doesn't</i></b></u>. The only control mechanism that the vinculum offers is Perfect Impression for Social Maneuvering. And there are specific rules on what to happen when one player tries to use Social Maneuvers on another player. Majesty and Dominate are far more worrisome in this case. Of course, the Beast can try to fight back at the mind control game with Siren's Song, Alien Allure, and You Must Obey.<br /> <br /> Really, I feel that you're overexaggerating the blood bonds. Has it been a problem in the game you're running yet, or is this something that you're afraid will happen? Because, if the latter, you might just be borrowing trouble unnecessarily. If the former, sit down and ask your group if its something that, as a whole, they're interested in exploring - its something that's a regular plot point in Vampire, and dealing with the perils of crossover is a major plot point for Beast. And go from there.<br /> <br /> EDIT - As well, mages bring up their own, separate complications into crossover. No, they can't really mind control anyone effectively until Mind 5 (you need Mind 4 to open all doors in a social maneuvering system). However, as glorified swiss army knives, they threaten to make others in the party redundant and hog the spotlight, which is a significant problem in its own right. They laugh at mystery stories that stump other supers. A mage player doesn't need to make a werewolf into a pet. They just start shaping the Shadow to suit their Obsessions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 08-23-2015, 01:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T10:49:28-07:00","id":637171,"title":"","content":"Seriously, in many games you can reach Perfect Impression with your group in no time just because of group dynamics. And even if you don't, what holds you from just Social Maneuvering your fellow PCs? The Blood Bond adds a descriptive emotion as fluff, but the only rule is to improve your Social Maneuvering against the target. Unless you think Social Maneuvering itself overpower, it is effectively impossible for Blood Bonds to be.<br /> <br /> At the time it takes to form a Blood Bond, a Mastigos will have enough of a sympathetic link to everyone as to mind control them from his house.<br /> <br /> If even with that you still worries, just house-rule the quantity of blood. Its far easier than messing with the roll mechanics. Y'know, you <u>can</u> determine that a few drops aren't enough, they need at least a cup, or that even with a few drops an entire point of Vitae still mystically retains the pungent smell and taste of blood.<br /> <br /> Given that you're willing to change the roll involved already, to argue that a cup of tea is an unavoidably perfect vessel makes no sense at all. Oh, and solves nothing, because then you can simply try again and again with no consequence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T11:19:44-07:00","id":637180,"title":"","content":"Besides, not everyone <i>likes</i> tea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T11:35:25-07:00","id":637187,"title":"","content":"If the Blood Bond is overpowered, Primal Allure (the Cunning Facet of the Gift of Dominance in Werewolf) must be broken in half. A starting werewolf character can force a Perfect Impression on anyone at any time without even needing to try to slip something into the subject's drink once, let alone on three separate occasions.<br /> <br /> In case it's not clear, what I'm getting at is that Vinculum is actually one of the weakest means vampires have for controlling other characters. It's outclassed by a werewolf ability, and werewolves are not even known for their mind control powers like vampires are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T12:59:20-07:00","id":637309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Araknee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/636546-2ed-blood-bonds-totally-overpowered?p=636894#post636894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my game, I would not accept a blood bond through a cup of tea of coffee. Let's see why:<br /> <br /> 1st, I absolutly now that vitae points and lethal points are abstract and I always thought that giving them numerical values as canon is wrong. But still, it can help us to evaluate proportions in relation to one another, while recognizing that the result should not be a strong golden rule.<br /> <br /> 2st, let's try to evaluate in real values what it means. 1 vitae = 1 lethal damage. You can kill a human by drinking him dry. An average human = 5 damage. An average human has also, from biological standarts, 5 to 6 liters of blood. We can approximately say that 1 vitae = 1 liter of blood. To avoid making this a canon, let's say it can depend from the narrative context (defined by the ST or a dialogic construction between ST and player), and that 1 vitae = +_ from 1/3 to 3 liters of blood. Generally, specially during the game, it's not useful to give real life numbers to these conceptual indicators, but let's do it here for the purpose. As a blood bond equals 1 vitae. It means that your cup of tea or coffee should contain at least, in our largest case, 1/3 liters. It means you don't have coffee in your cup, if you fill it with blood.<br /> <br /> 3st, vitae is not blood. It is a magical transformation of blood through the vampire's being. It has more potency. It has a magical taste. I would say that the blood does not liquefy easily in a liquid. One cannot dring half a cup of tea without knowing what he's drinking. The magical potency of the vitae is stronger that the blackness of your ethiopian coffee. Of course, there's the taste, the magical appealing to the taste of vitae. You feel you're drinking something very special, but you bloody know what it is : not blood, but something that you can directly categorizye to &quot;something f*kin weird that is link to human blood&quot;.<br /> <br /> These are to me 2 good reasons to make the blood bond a plot device (it is difficult to do it, it does not only require a good roll or a wise scene, it requires a whole machination if you don't physically or magically force your target). Btw, I would use the Social Maneuvering System before letting anything that has such a consequence on the game to go.<br /> <br /> With an exception of course : the blood bound the PC is making is really good for the story.</div> </div> </div> </div>I want to stop you right here because yes, vitae points are abstract because when a vampire sucks the lifeblood of someone, he's literally sucking their life along with the blood. The damage that the blood-doll suffers isn't exclusively blood loss. It's her life slipping away to sustain the undead monstrosity feeding from her.<br /> <br /> The above is evidenced by the fact that an elder vampire with above average blood potency can hold more vitae than a neonate. Vampires don't become literally bloated corpses with the blood of their victims, they simply can hold more life within their stolen blood.<br /> <br /> There is also the fact that if every hunger frenzied vampire would leave completely corpses, they would have raised many an eyebrow in the investigation that follow. This is not the case.<br /> <br /> Nevermind that diablerie literally steals the victim's soul.<br /> <br /> Last but not least, just imagine the kind of force that would be needed to actually drain a human body from all it's blood in under 30 seconds.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","user":"Ephsy","date":". 08-23-2015, 04:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T13:50:02-07:00","id":637353,"title":"","content":"I suppose I should point out that the books say Social Maneuvering should not be used on player character, only storyteller characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T14:06:49-07:00","id":637369,"title":"","content":"What I've learned from this thread is that coffee is overpowered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T14:16:01-07:00","id":637378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/636546-2ed-blood-bonds-totally-overpowered?p=637187#post637187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In case it's not clear, what I'm getting at is that Vinculum is actually one of the weakest means vampires have for controlling other characters. It's outclassed by a werewolf ability, and werewolves are not even known for their mind control powers like vampires are.</div> </div> </div> </div> To be fair, Primal Allure doesn't grant stop someone from attacking you like a Vinculum does or give you a mental discipline boost, though, so its not -quite- the same. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T14:28:18-07:00","id":637389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/636546-2ed-blood-bonds-totally-overpowered?p=637378#post637378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> To be fair, Primal Allure doesn't grant stop someone from attacking you like a Vinculum does or give you a mental discipline boost, though, so its not -quite- the same. </div> </div> </div> </div>True, true.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T14:40:25-07:00","id":637401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/636546-2ed-blood-bonds-totally-overpowered?p=637309#post637309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Last but not least, just imagine the kind of force that would be needed to actually drain a human body from all it's blood in under 30 seconds.</div> </div> </div> </div>Presumably it would be less than the force required to create an asolar powered perpetual parasite that ignores decay as well as entropy. I get your point but come on, magic.<br /> <br /> Fortunately the writers have left this bit up in the air. While some may complain, I'm not saying you are, I see it as an opportunity handed to us to use it our own way. So that if you want your vampires to have fangs-as-straws sucking blood out of people until they buckle inward like a Capri-Sun pouch, they might, while others might have the fangs as bleeding implements, leading to an awful lot of lapping and sucking at spilled blood.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/636546-2ed-blood-bonds-totally-overpowered?p=637378#post637378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> To be fair, Primal Allure doesn't grant stop someone from attacking you like a Vinculum does or give you a mental discipline boost, though, so its not -quite- the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also wyrdhamster's issue is with all vampires having this as a natural ability, making the comparison to gauru's healing more accurate, providing one believes in balance in a storytelling game in the first place. Though the social bonuses gained from a blood bond can be imitated by any template, even mortals, with simple good manners and a charming personality.<br /> <br /> What it comes down to for me is that the concept of balance, the way wyrdhamster is using it, is laughable. We're not playing a wargame, where everyone comes to the table to fight each other with equal odds of winning because of a point system. And it's not a MOBA, with vampires and werewolves being put in a white room with tables full of tea. It's a storytelling game. If your character got blood bonded your character got blood bonded, if you or your storyteller view that as the end of the game, outside of special circumstances, you're doing it wrong. I hate saying that because it's really hard to do the game wrong, you have to go out of your way to do it. If your character can't kill another character in a single blow, be glad it's a storytelling game and he's not getting any extra experience for killing folks and your character isn't underpowered, just not able to kill people in a single blow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-23-2015, 05:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T14:59:16-07:00","id":637421,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure the [health] vitae a vampire can suck from you doesn't take <i>all</i> your blood with it, because at that point you can still be revived with a medicine roll and 2 days bed rest. That doesn't happen if you're bone dry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T15:18:55-07:00","id":637444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/636546-2ed-blood-bonds-totally-overpowered?p=637421#post637421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure the [health] vitae a vampire can suck from you doesn't take <i>all</i> your blood with it, because at that point you can still be revived with a medicine roll and 2 days bed rest. That doesn't happen if you're bone dry.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, being full on lethal damage leaves you unconscious and you upgrade your leftmost wound to aggravated every turn until someone stabilizes you with a Medicine roll.. That upgrade to Agg is supposed to represent bleeding out, which indicates to me that you must have at least <i>some</i> blood left to lose, at least until your health track is full on Agg. Even then, you're not necessarily bone dry, you've just lost too much blood to stay alive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T16:21:19-07:00","id":637506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/636546-2ed-blood-bonds-totally-overpowered?p=637401#post637401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Presumably it would be less than the force required to create an asolar powered perpetual parasite that ignores decay as well as entropy. I get your point but come on, magic.<br /> <br /> Fortunately the writers have left this bit up in the air. While some may complain, I'm not saying you are, I see it as an opportunity handed to us to use it our own way. So that if you want your vampires to have fangs-as-straws sucking blood out of people until they buckle inward like a Capri-Sun pouch, they might, while others might have the fangs as bleeding implements, leading to an awful lot of lapping and sucking at spilled blood.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, go ahead and disregard all the other points I raised.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T17:26:59-07:00","id":637553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/636546-2ed-blood-bonds-totally-overpowered?p=637506#post637506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sure, go ahead and disregard all the other points I raised.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't have any argument with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T17:33:08-07:00","id":637559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/636546-2ed-blood-bonds-totally-overpowered?p=637353#post637353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose I should point out that the books say Social Maneuvering should not be used on player character, only storyteller characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually it says to only use it with approval from the target's player.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T22:47:01-07:00","id":637729,"title":"","content":"The blood bond isn't slavery. It's powerful, it's affecting, after a while it starts to feel like love. But the potential thrall's will remains free. It's his judgment that's compromised.<br /> <br /> Sometimes you can't be angry at someone you love. Other times you couldn't be angrier at anyone else. The Vinculum isn't an automatic ticket to good vibes. It's a bond. It ties you together. It's hard to shake. If I'm feeling romantic I might say that in a pinch it'll always come through.<br /> <br /> Some sires think it's safer to bond their childer. They're betting on that bond -- that when they're staked out for the sun, their childer won't, can't leave them behind. But night to night, a thrall is only as likely to obey her regnant as anyone else she cares about. It may be an insane, obsessive sort of care. It may lead to bad decisions and crazy risks. But when the sun's peeking over the horizon, sometimes selfishness wins out over love. Sometimes work is more important, or God, or sometimes you just love someone else more, tricks of the blood be damned.<br /> <br /> The blood bond is a tool, an advantage, a way to manipulate people, and it's a powerful one. With finesse, a vampire can use it to get what she wants, to keep your heart on a string and the rest of you on a leash. But it doesn't carry the surety of Dominate or the easy trust of Majesty. It brings you together, but what happens when you meet is still up to the chaos of emotions and hormones and rationalizations. It's love, and love takes work.<br /> <br /> You <i>can </i>defy your regnant. But you'll have a hell of a time walking away.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":2,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","user":"Rose Bailey","date":". 08-24-2015, 01:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T23:14:20-07:00","id":637732,"title":"","content":"It was a Masquerade game, but I got threefold bonded to another player character once. My character(A Giovanni) knew the other guy did it as a way to manipulate him and control him, but golly gosh, he thought it was such a clever trick-but at the same time it demonstrated that the other guy did not really have a good sense of who should be making the choices. It got to a point where I decided that the best thing I could do was stake the guy and put him in a safe place while taking over his affairs-added benefit, I could show him the dangers of my attention and attraction.<br /> <br /> It didn't happen, but if I played that character better, the other guy could very easily have come to regret the closeness of our characters. He might still.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-24T03:19:16-07:00","id":637822,"title":"","content":"And that because the Bond is even more powerful in Masquerade. No rolls to resist whatsoever, and you have to spend willpower just to consider acting against you Regnant's interests. But even then, it was far from overpowered. I played bonded characters, and bonded other characters sometimes, and it never spoiled the game. Actually, one thing I learned is that a good Regnant should work extra-cautious and be nice with the bonded, because things can get nasty for her in no time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-24T09:30:23-07:00","id":638106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/636546-2ed-blood-bonds-totally-overpowered?p=637559#post637559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually it says to only use it with approval from the target's player.</div> </div> </div> </div>I said &quot;should&quot; not &quot;can't&quot; but if you add our two points together you get an unstated optional rule which makes the criticism on blood bonds moot on inter-player social interaction. Social maneuvering used on player characters is optional.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-24T11:43:05-07:00","id":638237,"title":"","content":"Plus, WoD games are cooperative, not antagonistic. I would assume that the party, despite being different splats, want to get along and not try to screw each other over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-24T12:59:24-07:00","id":638275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/636546-2ed-blood-bonds-totally-overpowered?p=638237#post638237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus, WoD games are cooperative, not antagonistic. I would assume that the party, despite being different splats, want to get along and not try to screw each other over.</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely this. I've never enjoyed a game where we were all aimed against each other. I'm not saying conflict can't happen in group, but the most satisfying conflict came from forces driving us to tear the group apart because we all wanted our own individual things, but we fought the other way just as much because we wanted to stay together as a cobblethought family too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-24T17:05:38-07:00","id":638489,"title":"","content":"Though I wouldn't say nWoD IS cooperative (but rather that it can be both), it is a reasonable default assumption.<br /> <br /> I see little reason to fear the Blood Bond on a cooperative game, and most shall be.<br /> <br /> And even LESS reason in an antagonistic game, because then you can be sure no one will simply have tea at the other's house without worrying about mystical poisons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-24T17:40:37-07:00","id":638516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/636546-2ed-blood-bonds-totally-overpowered?p=638489#post638489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though I wouldn't say nWoD IS cooperative (but rather that it can be both), it is a reasonable default assumption.<br /> <br /> I see little reason to fear the Blood Bond on a cooperative game, and most shall be.<br /> <br /> And even LESS reason in an antagonistic game, because then you can be sure no one will simply have tea at the other's house without worrying about mystical poisons.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was not familiar with Vampire and blood bonds and all the ways one could be bonded, and the other player was a Tremere.<br /> <br /> I got fuuuucked.(But, in fairness, apparently I scared his superior enough to make him give the order <i>to</i> blood bond me. It wasn't douchery.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 08-24-2015, 08:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-24T23:17:56-07:00","id":638845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/636546-2ed-blood-bonds-totally-overpowered?p=638237#post638237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus, WoD games are cooperative, not antagonistic. I would assume that the party, despite being different splats, want to get along and not try to screw each other over.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel it varies from gameline to gameline. Vampire can quite easily lean into quite antagonistic territory more easily than something like say, Hunter or Werewolf could. Crossover games can range the full spectrum very easily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1462,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","user":"Xenesis","date":". 08-25-2015, 02:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-25T01:03:46-07:00","id":638867,"title":"","content":"Developer as always in to the point...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/636546-2ed-blood-bonds-totally-overpowered?p=637729#post637729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The blood bond isn't slavery. It's powerful, it's affecting, after a while it starts to feel like love. But the potential thrall's will remains free. It's his judgment that's compromised.<br /> <br /> Sometimes you can't be angry at someone you love. Other times you couldn't be angrier at anyone else. The Vinculum isn't an automatic ticket to good vibes. It's a bond. It ties you together. It's hard to shake. If I'm feeling romantic I might say that in a pinch it'll always come through.<br /> <br /> Some sires think it's safer to bond their childer. They're betting on that bond -- that when they're staked out for the sun, their childer won't, can't leave them behind. But night to night, a thrall is only as likely to obey her regnant as anyone else she cares about. It may be an insane, obsessive sort of care. It may lead to bad decisions and crazy risks. But when the sun's peeking over the horizon, sometimes selfishness wins out over love. Sometimes work is more important, or God, or sometimes you just love someone else more, tricks of the blood be damned.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, <b>Rose</b>, I see now that Blood Bonds in <b>Requiem</b> are like Maker-Child relationship in the <i>True Blood</i> - they are, simple, love. With all the pros and cons of it... Regent do not <b>own you</b>, you just want to please him. The only real question is how much it is the Heather plot line from Bloodlines cRPG?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=U5Q98oCaYPc\" data-code=\"U5Q98oCaYPc\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/U5Q98oCaYPc/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> How different <b>Requiem</b>'s Blood Bonds from this video?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/636546-2ed-blood-bonds-totally-overpowered?p=637729#post637729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The blood bond is a tool, an advantage, a way to manipulate people, and it's a powerful one. With finesse, a vampire can use it to get what she wants, to keep your heart on a string and the rest of you on a leash. But it doesn't carry the surety of Dominate or the easy trust of Majesty. It brings you together, but what happens when you meet is still up to the chaos of emotions and hormones and rationalizations. It's love, and love takes work.<br /> <br /> You <i>can </i>defy your regnant. But you'll have a hell of a time walking away.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mine screw opinion maybe stir from our gameplay where PC Daeva vampire with Majesty 3 Blood Bonded every other PCs - but it still was kind a bad, by my RAW reading of <b>Requiem</b> 2ED.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/636546-2ed-blood-bonds-totally-overpowered?p=637822#post637822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that because the Bond is even more powerful in Masquerade. No rolls to resist whatsoever, and you have to spend willpower just to consider acting against you Regnant's interests. But even then, it was far from overpowered. I played bonded characters, and bonded other characters sometimes, and it never spoiled the game. Actually, one thing I learned is that a good Regnant should work extra-cautious and be nice with the bonded, because things can get nasty for her in no time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably we run it bad, as I'm not <b>Requiem</b> ST and other Vampire STs in club are all from <b>Masquerade </b>- and I ask them on advice to run it. Very much would help me pointing differences between Blood Bonds in <b>Masquerade</b> and <b>Requiem</b>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-25T04:21:06-07:00","id":638928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/636546-2ed-blood-bonds-totally-overpowered?p=638867#post638867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How different <b>Requiem</b>'s Blood Bonds from this video?</div> </div> </div> </div> It is absolutely a drug, and the high is the best there is, better than any street or pharmaceutical drug. The rest? It can depend on the person - some people have highly addictive natures and naturally are drawn to others like that. The woman in this case is stalkerish. She could have been naturally inclined to this behavior, but never had the opertunity before. So, some people -could- act like that. Not all of them will, but its possible.<br /> <br /> I mean, brush with the supernatural, and suddenly disappears? Obsession is actually a pretty standard reaction in the WoD, so thus, the Masquerade, given that obsession may become hunter-ish. Combine that with the effects of the Kiss (you do feed on Heather), the drug addiction, and the whole savior-stockholm syndrome Heather is likely experiencing, yeah, that's viable for some people. The thing is that its not just the vinculum driving the ghoul, its a combination of several factors. &quot;Make me feel this way&quot; is a dead give away for being an addict.<br /> <br /> To be honest, even one drink in Masquerade or 1e Requiem didn't have that huge of an impact on people, which suggests that Heather would have gone this route if someone addicted her to other kinds of drugs.<br /> <br /> Plus, for as much fun as Masquerade was to play, it wasn't exactly the feminist game of the year - Heather is more than a bit sexualized, and should be considered in no small part fetish fuel. Half the women in the game you meet are like that.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 08-25-2015, 07:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-25T17:15:09-07:00","id":639606,"title":"","content":"Heather gives a lot of giveaways to be overdependent, thirst for attention and lonely all by herself. I'd bet she would be almost that way for a hug.<br /> <br /> In the end, in both games the Bond have the same description, and it doesn't change the bonded's personality. It uses this personality, instead.<br /> <br /> About distinction, it was one of rules. In Masquerade the Bond is automatic (3 times and done, no resist rolls) and demands willpower to go against the Regnant's interests. The same effect, other rules altogether.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T15:00:57-07:00","id":640679,"title":"","content":"<i>Bloodlines</i> is a stylized portrayal of <i>Masquerad</i><i>e</i>. So Heather isn't just a ghoul, isn't just a blood bond-ee, she's almost a caricature of those things. She's presented in the neediest possible terms, because she's the game's one shot at really showing the ghoul-regnant relationship. And usually, even with all the addiction metaphors we get into in <i>Requiem</i>, neither ghouls nor the bonded are quite like that.<br /> <br /> EDIT: By the way, &quot;stylized&quot; and &quot;caricature&quot; are by no means me taking shots at <i>Bloodlines</i>. There are some problems with it, but it's a great game, and has been influential on my views regarding both <i>Vampire</i> games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":2,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","user":"Rose Bailey","date":". 08-26-2015, 06:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T18:38:13-07:00","id":640889,"title":"","content":"I believe the book states that the Blood Bond is one of, if not the most potent ability the Vitae possesses. But even still, it does have its drawbacks.<br /> <br /> In order to form a blood bond, the subject has to drink the blood of the same vampire on three separate nights, which means that forming even one bond is a time consuming ordeal and requires a lot of planning unless you just chain somebody up for 72 hours and force feed them. Second of all, they need to drink your blood at least once a year to maintain the bond. For any non-vampires, if the master is destroyed, the bond is broken instantly. It's only fellow vampires who appear to be compelled to follow orders after the destruction of their regent.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind how powerful a Werewolf or a Mage is compared to a vampire. You don't even have to be Arch Master in order to literally nuke somebody as a proper Mage. Just have a handy knowledge of science and the right blend of magic, and Mages seem more OP than any other splat.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Blood Bond is a powerful, dangerous ability, this is true. But it is also risky and a constant effort to maintain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T18:41:15-07:00","id":640893,"title":"","content":"In my first session of Werewolf second edition my guy got stabbed in the chest with a syringe full of a cocktail of tranquilizers and Vitae by an invisible vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T18:45:24-07:00","id":640910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/636546-2ed-blood-bonds-totally-overpowered?p=640893#post640893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my first session of Werewolf second edition my guy got stabbed in the chest with a syringe full of a cocktail of tranquilizers and Vitae by an invisible vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Congratulations. Now let's see the vamp pull it off two more times. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T18:56:58-07:00","id":640953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/636546-2ed-blood-bonds-totally-overpowered?p=640910#post640910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Congratulations. Now let's see the vamp pull it off two more times. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that would not have worked out so well. The first time he was mostly surprised that things like vampires existed, or at least that people walked around smelling so strongly of blood and such, the realization that she was a vampire came shortly afterward. Then later he found the vampire in a sticky predicament and decided to help her out of it. They hit it off better and he learned about a local hunter group and a strange covenant and a nearby town that's run by vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T19:50:59-07:00","id":641005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/636546-2ed-blood-bonds-totally-overpowered?p=640889#post640889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe the book states that the Blood Bond is one of, if not the most potent ability the Vitae possesses. But even still, it does have its drawbacks.<br /> <br /> In order to form a blood bond, the subject has to drink the blood of the same vampire on three separate nights, which means that forming even one bond is a time consuming ordeal and requires a lot of planning unless you just chain somebody up for 72 hours and force feed them. Second of all, they need to drink your blood at least once a year to maintain the bond. For any non-vampires, if the master is destroyed, the bond is broken instantly. It's only fellow vampires who appear to be compelled to follow orders after the destruction of their regent.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind how powerful a Werewolf or a Mage is compared to a vampire. You don't even have to be Arch Master in order to literally nuke somebody as a proper Mage. Just have a handy knowledge of science and the right blend of magic, and Mages seem more OP than any other splat.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Blood Bond is a powerful, dangerous ability, this is true. But it is also risky and a constant effort to maintain.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm a little confused by this post. To my knowledge in VtR 2e:<br /> <br /> 1. The bond is formed after one dose unless you are both a vampire and capable of resisting. The third-stage bond makes you immune to all others, but you are bound from the first dose.<br /> <br /> 2. Where does it say that death ends the bond? This discussion was had in another thread, and what I gathered from that thread and the book was that it never says death breaks the bond, let alone specifying that it does for some and not for others.<br /> <br /> 3. The bond makes you pliable, as discussed earlier in the thread. Nobody is compelled.<br /> <br /> Is your post referring to a different edition, or is there text that I've missed somewhere?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T22:47:34-07:00","id":641158,"title":"","content":"I think this post talked more about Masquerade's bond. But both are bonds from the first drop, even if weak bonds.<br /> <br /> Actually, in that I concede, Requiem did the first bonds stronger than in Masquerade. In Masquerade they had no mechanical effect whatsoever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T09:16:08-07:00","id":641718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/636546-2ed-blood-bonds-totally-overpowered?p=641005#post641005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'm a little confused by this post. To my knowledge in VtR 2e:<br /> <br /> 1. The bond is formed after one dose unless you are both a vampire and capable of resisting. The third-stage bond makes you immune to all others, but you are bound from the first dose.<br /> <br /> 2. Where does it say that death ends the bond? This discussion was had in another thread, and what I gathered from that thread and the book was that it never says death breaks the bond, let alone specifying that it does for some and not for others.<br /> <br /> 3. The bond makes you pliable, as discussed earlier in the thread. Nobody is compelled.<br /> <br /> Is your post referring to a different edition, or is there text that I've missed somewhere?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Maybe the blood bond got a revamp (heh) in 2nd edition, but in 1st the bond worked like this<br /> <br /> 1st stage - No compulsion is manifested yet, although the subject does feel subconsciously drawn to follow the vampire around. They just keep appearing in the same place by coincidence.<br /> <br /> 2nd stage - The subject begins to perceive the vampire as a friend, although is still not outright compelled to follow orders.<br /> <br /> 3rd stage - The subject becomes a slave to the vampire's will.<br /> <br /> <br /> And in regards to severing the bond, the book clearly stated that death of the master would sever the bond, but said there were accounts of fellow vampires continuing to fulfill their master's will after they were destroyed. The length of time for doing so varied from one individual to the next.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T09:54:12-07:00","id":641753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/636546-2ed-blood-bonds-totally-overpowered?p=640893#post640893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my first session of Werewolf second edition my guy got stabbed in the chest with a syringe full of a cocktail of tranquilizers and Vitae by an invisible vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does this count with regards to blood bonds? If I remember correctly, the rules state that the victim has to <b>drink</b> the vitae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1125-gflash","name":"gflash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1125_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T10:02:13-07:00","id":641758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gflash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/636546-2ed-blood-bonds-totally-overpowered?p=641753#post641753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does this count with regards to blood bonds? If I remember correctly, the rules state that the victim has to <b>drink</b> the vitae.</div> </div> </div> </div>Strictly by the book, no, though there's an example of it being communicated by a spit to the eye, and the developer said lacing drugs with it would work. In the end, the storyteller makes the rules, and thats what they decided. Since he was briefly incapacitated she could have just shoved some in my character's mouth, though that wouldn't have ended well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T10:12:57-07:00","id":641784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/636546-2ed-blood-bonds-totally-overpowered?p=641758#post641758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Strictly by the book, no, though there's an example of it being communicated by a spit to the eye, and the developer said lacing drugs with it would work. In the end, the storyteller makes the rules, and thats what they decided. Since he was briefly incapacitated she could have just shoved some in my character's mouth, though that wouldn't have ended well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Blood <i>kuruth</i> trigger, eh?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T10:21:32-07:00","id":641789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/636546-2ed-blood-bonds-totally-overpowered?p=641784#post641784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blood <i>kuruth</i> trigger, eh?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it would have just been more invasive, when he came up on her later he'd have probably killed her, or let her pursuers kill her. When I started I couldn't think of a trigger appropriate for the character, so we let it slide for the first couple sessions. It really took me a while to get into him, he was meant to be cold and disconnected, but ended up being smart and ridiculously impulsive, which is a horrible mix.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-27-2015, 01:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T01:28:59-07:00","id":642730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/636546-2ed-blood-bonds-totally-overpowered?p=641718#post641718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe the blood bond got a revamp (heh) in 2nd edition, but in 1st the bond worked like this<br /> <br /> 1st stage - No compulsion is manifested yet, although the subject does feel subconsciously drawn to follow the vampire around. They just keep appearing in the same place by coincidence.<br /> <br /> 2nd stage - The subject begins to perceive the vampire as a friend, although is still not outright compelled to follow orders.<br /> <br /> 3rd stage - The subject becomes a slave to the vampire's will.<br /> <br /> <br /> And in regards to severing the bond, the book clearly stated that death of the master would sever the bond, but said there were accounts of fellow vampires continuing to fulfill their master's will after they were destroyed. The length of time for doing so varied from one individual to the next.</div> </div> </div> </div>The bond did got revamped in 2nd ed.<br /> <br /> Now, though here are still fluff indicating the same degrees of obsession, the mechanics become clear in the effects, relating to the Social Maneuvering system.<br /> <br /> Each drop causes an improvement of +X in Impression and a reduce of -X in number of Doors, plus +X bonus dice in social rolls against the target (no powers covered, though). Just toss the number of stages in those Xs and you got most of it. How you interpret the fluff can actually change how the Social Maneuvering works, since you can change the actual interests of the target, but it is completely at ST or Player discretion. No Soc-Man rule is really changed.<br /> <br /> And the bond ends in 1 year, give or take, all the stages vanishing at once. You need blood to restart the time countdown.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T04:55:55-07:00","id":642842,"title":"","content":"The bonus in social rolls also extends to Disciplines aimed at the thrall.<br /> <br /> And at the full Vinculum, with a three stage blood bond, your disciplines last longer against the thrall. ' Lastly, all of the regnant\u2019s lingering Discipline effects gain additional duration. Any Discipline that would last a scene lasts one night. Any that last a night instead last a week. One week becomes one month. One month becomes one year.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T12:01:24-07:00","id":644461,"title":"","content":"Next time I'll look in the book before writing, thanks.<br /> <br /> But still, 2nd ed made clearer rules and put some benefit on lesser bonds.<br /> <br /> It also made the bond resistible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T12:22:06-07:00","id":644485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/636546-2ed-blood-bonds-totally-overpowered?p=644461#post644461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also made the bond resistible.</div> </div> </div> </div>I still think that using only Blood Potence (and equivalent ) is to potent on this. Much more I would be inclined in the run it as Resolve + Blood Potency roll...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T13:15:22-07:00","id":644564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/636546-2ed-blood-bonds-totally-overpowered?p=644485#post644485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I still think that using only Blood Potence (and equivalent ) is to potent on this. Much more I would be inclined in the run it as Resolve + Blood Potency roll...</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the idea is supposed to be that against mortals it just straight-up works. This way you've got to be a supernatural creature (or have some external source of supernatural tolerance) to roll better than a chance die to resist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T15:36:18-07:00","id":644666,"title":"","content":"The book in fact says &quot;mortals have no such defense.&quot; I think it is safe to say that anything with an equivalent to a Blood Potency stat can use Willpower to resist a blood bond in the same way as Kindred.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T15:43:00-07:00","id":644667,"title":"","content":"The real question is do <i>ghouls</i> get a roll? They do have a blood potency score now. It's just zero.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T16:27:44-07:00","id":644707,"title":"","content":"They could only get a chance roll and would always start out with a first stage bond when they are made into a ghoul. I guess they might then have an advantage over mortals when ghouls are in withdrawal. I suspect they aren't supposed to get a roll, but I'm not seeing how rolls always limited to chance die are significant either way when they are frequent. I always assume ghouls that have been around a while and don't have lots of masters are fully bound.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T16:32:10-07:00","id":644711,"title":"","content":"Since ghouls need at least one Vitae a month to remain a ghoul, and a blood bond doesn't dissipate for a year, most ghouls will likely have a full blood bond eventually.<br /> <br /> But the actual section says, 'Your character gains the Blood Potency trait at 0, allowing him to store and spend Vitae.' Which suggests they can't use it for other things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-30T03:35:25-07:00","id":645216,"title":"","content":"I would rule for Ghouls having a chance die, though it isn't clear, indeed.<br /> <br /> And I strongly suggest against doing it better than Power Trait. It IS supposed to be hard to resist, if at all possible. The logistical difficulties of a Blood Bond are already steep. Making it reasonably resistible will make it almost useless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-30T05:45:20-07:00","id":645305,"title":"","content":"I can't remember, but was it posible to use Willpower to boost the roll? If so a clued in Ghoul could roll 3 dice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-30T05:57:18-07:00","id":645313,"title":"","content":"You need to spend willpower to roll at all, so no.<br /> <br /> Although even if you could you get a penalty equal to the number of vitae ingested, so even if it didn't they'd only get 2 dice at most.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-01T05:10:27-07:00","id":647870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/636546-2ed-blood-bonds-totally-overpowered?p=644485#post644485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I still think that using only Blood Potence (and equivalent ) is to potent on this. Much more I would be inclined in the run it as Resolve + Blood Potency roll...</div> </div> </div> </div>So change it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}